\begin{beyond}
\textbf{A closed form for $S$.} The sum $S=\sum_{m=2,4,6,\dots}m^2/(m^2-1)^5$ equals $(15-\pi^2)\pi^2/3072$. Deriving this requires partial fractions together with known values of sums of inverse powers of integers, techniques this book does not develop (see \cite{rhb}). We take the closed form on trust; Problem~22 checks it numerically, and nothing in this chapter depends on it.
\end{beyond}
